cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use citracer in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "citracer"
abstract: >-
  citracer traces citation chains for any keyword across research papers.
  Given a PDF and a keyword, it finds every sentence where the keyword appears,
  identifies the references cited nearby, downloads those papers and repeats
  the process recursively, producing an interactive citation graph. A reverse
  mode walks forward through the papers that cite the source while mentioning
  the keyword.
authors:
  - family-names: "Pinet"
    given-names: "Marc"
version: "1.8.1"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/marcpinet/citracer"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcpinet/citracer"
keywords:
  - citation-graph
  - literature-review
  - grobid
  - arxiv
  - semantic-scholar
  - openreview
  - pdf-parsing
  - research-tools
  - bibliography
